(2786444, 386998, 811, '<td valign="top">Simply lovely.  I am not usually a fan of IR, but it is shots like this that make me want to learn more about it.  I love the *color* tones in this and the composition is strong as well.</td>', 'Simply lovely.  I am not usually a fan of IR, but it is shots like this that make me want to learn more about it.  I love the *color* tones in this and the composition is strong as well.', '2006-09-02 01:32:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2786508, 385067, 5885, '<td valign="top">Awwwww... look at (him/her?) Chihuahua puppies are just soo cute. This might even be cuter than my Kirby. :-)<br/> <br/>I''m not voting... but let me offer some critique.<br/> <br/>I''ve like that you have used a solid background. But the texture of the background is a bit distracting. Also, I think a pink would have gone better with the "scene" you are going for.<br/> <br/>Also, looks like you are using an on-camera flash. I''m guessing from the depth of field is probably a point and shoot camera. There are ways to diffuse the flash some. One very effective way is to place a pingpong ball over the flash, allowing it to diffuse the light some. Also wax paper can diffuse it also.<br/> <br/>He''s still just too darn cute though. :-)</td>', 'Awwwww... look at (him/her?) Chihuahua puppies are just soo cute. This might even be cuter than my Kirby. :-) I''m not voting... but let me offer some critique. I''ve like that you have used a solid background. But the texture of the background is a bit distracting. Also, I think a pink would have gone better with the "scene" you are going for. Also, looks like you are using an on-camera flash. I''m guessing from the depth of field is probably a point and shoot camera. There are ways to diffuse the flash some. One very effective way is to place a pingpong ball over the flash, allowing it to diffuse the light some. Also wax paper can diffuse it also. He''s still just too darn cute though. :-)', '2006-09-02 01:50:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2786510, 386095, 5885, '<td valign="top">Hehe, I like it :-) One suggestion: I think a slightly different angle with more of the back of the child''s head and moving the mirror over to the right side of the image would have made a stronger composition.<br/> <br/>Not voting, but if I were, I''d give you a 6 as is.</td>', 'Hehe, I like it :-) One suggestion: I think a slightly different angle with more of the back of the child''s head and moving the mirror over to the right side of the image would have made a stronger composition. Not voting, but if I were, I''d give you a 6 as is.', '2006-09-02 01:52:25.000000', NULL, 1),
