(2790336, 387766, 43115, '<td valign="top">I haven''t seen the movie, but I''ll assume this is relevant.<br/> <br/>Great use of space and composition.  Technically a very sound photo.  I like the "letterboxing" that you (and a few others) did to give it that movie still feel.  Great job!</td>', 'I haven''t seen the movie, but I''ll assume this is relevant. Great use of space and composition.  Technically a very sound photo.  I like the "letterboxing" that you (and a few others) did to give it that movie still feel.  Great job!', '2006-09-02 22:45:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790338, 385891, 59564, '<td valign="top">If this is referring to the version with Streisand, the goatee is throwin me off :)  Nice choice with the b&amp;w. I think it adds more emotion than the color version would.  Cropping at the waist level (or maybe a little below) may have added a little more intimacy between the viewer and the photo. Overall I think this is a great photo.  Good luck!</td>', 'If this is referring to the version with Streisand, the goatee is throwin me off :)  Nice choice with the b&w. I think it adds more emotion than the color version would.  Cropping at the waist level (or maybe a little below) may have added a little more intimacy between the viewer and the photo. Overall I think this is a great photo.  Good luck!', '2006-09-02 22:46:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790345, 387539, 62187, '<td valign="top">No way!!!! Nobody has ever heard of this movie. No way! It''s the best movie in the world. When the little boy disappears in the jungle...unimaginalble to a father and mother. Then the dad looks for the boy for years and years never giving up. Amazingly he finds his son. But, the boy calls him daddy and not father because he was raised by the native people and that''s what he knows. Yes, It was a great movie...thanks! 10</td>', 'No way!!!! Nobody has ever heard of this movie. No way! It''s the best movie in the world. When the little boy disappears in the jungle...unimaginalble to a father and mother. Then the dad looks for the boy for years and years never giving up. Amazingly he finds his son. But, the boy calls him daddy and not father because he was raised by the native people and that''s what he knows. Yes, It was a great movie...thanks! 10', '2006-09-02 22:47:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2790346, 387971, 38706, '<td valign="top">I think this would be stringer if the end of the pistol was visable.</td>', 'I think this would be stringer if the end of the pistol was visable.', '2006-09-02 22:47:53.000000', NULL, 1),
