(2828342, 387460, 332, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/>Hi Monica,<br/>First of all. I just love the film Amelie! The first thing I see is that the picture is just 564px instead of the full 640px. Larger size makes a better picture. People here on dpc ar pretty harsh and are not happy if the size isn''t the full size. I really like the black top/bottom frame. I get the feeling it is just taken just out of the film. I like the lighting in it. Good luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Best regards, Arni</td>', 'Critique Club:Hi Monica,First of all. I just love the film Amelie! The first thing I see is that the picture is just 564px instead of the full 640px. Larger size makes a better picture. People here on dpc ar pretty harsh and are not happy if the size isn''t the full size. I really like the black top/bottom frame. I get the feeling it is just taken just out of the film. I like the lighting in it. Good luck in future challenges. Best regards, Arni', '2006-09-12 17:00:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2828374, 387721, 332, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/>Hey Michael,<br/>Congrats on top 10 finish. I like this picture. It is well taken. The lighting is just great. The composition is good. I really like the wet hand. There is nothing that I see that could have been better. Maby in high contrast bw? Good luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Best regards, Arni</td>', 'Critique Club:Hey Michael,Congrats on top 10 finish. I like this picture. It is well taken. The lighting is just great. The composition is good. I really like the wet hand. There is nothing that I see that could have been better. Maby in high contrast bw? Good luck in future challenges. Best regards, Arni', '2006-09-12 17:12:47.000000', NULL, 0),
